// REALIZATION-CHECK-FORM-W1-W8-010 -- PROPOSED vocabulary successor; status atoms are operators.
// SUPERSEDES -009 SHA256 FDF53B6654C807B13540F087AC515FF9D5FD0C5F8EE54C30FAC6C9ABDA48E4A6 (PROMOTED).
// GOVERNED BY SPEC-MAL-TIG-DISPOSITION-001 v0.3.0 (V15) and Devon's DECIDE of 2026-10-16 ("go"):
// the three retired labels are names with NO operator behind them, in either column.
// ONE change: every status atom that -009 spelled with the retired passing label becomes "IF_THEN".
// That covers two columns -009 carried under one name: the W1..W8 statuses and the declaration and
// argument statuses (column R, per-test readings that meet into the reading byte), and the W8 route
// table dispositions copied from the engine (column D). NO reading byte changes: the meet still
// emits 19 / 0 / unexecuted exactly as -009 did, so EVERY promoted CHECK_FORM vector reproduces.
// The diagnostic wrapper prints the atoms, so a -010 diagnostic prints IF_THEN where -009 printed
// the retired label. Namespace renamed realization_check_form_w1_w8_010. The historical -009
// header and construction comments follow unchanged except where they named the vocabulary (-010).
// REALIZATION-CHECK-FORM-W1-W8-009 — PROPOSED correction for independent M3 and M5.
// Preserves -008 SHA256 2A4F1732C033B7DE28CDBE1DCF64E6C5DA76029F216534A11C25D45728708DF0.
// 002 W7: exact expected bytes OR a digest is sufficient; neither is mandatory over the other.
// expected_bytes [decimal bytes] supplies the closed payload, including the empty payload.
// If bytes and digest are both declared, sha256.mal computes their relation. NOT_SAME -> NO.
// The same comparison checks a reading byte against a declared digest. A proved mismatch reads NO.
// Missing/malformed declarations stay MAYBE; a witnessed contradiction dominates that gap.
// All source, claims and comparison witnesses remain separate from vector execution and TIG.
// Historical construction comments follow; this header supersedes -008's missing byte support.
// REALIZATION-CHECK-FORM-W1-W8-008 — PROPOSED explicit vector identity/output witnesses.
// Preserves -007 SHA256 40A6EE1FB6AEBCA7D100EFB09ABADFA395C8528E28E49D45885A7D35DED010BC.
// Each argument_N NAME sha256 HEX line binds the one-based position and normalized source name.
// Argument names are token sequences with boundaries, case-folded as in the existing comment reader.
// Claims are local to their declaration. Equal repeats HOLD; digest/name contradictions read NO.
// Missing, malformed, orphan or out-of-range associations remain MAYBE. Hash counts never bind.
// expected_sha256 HEX witnesses exact expected bytes by identity, separately from input identities.
// The expected digest is not a reading opcode. Missing evidence MAYBE; conflicting digests NO.
// A reading-name plus expected-digest claim remains MAYBE pending cross-representation comparison.
// SHA256_IDENTITY_DECLARATION defines identity, not a fresh read of an external preimage.
// This form reader discharges declarations; it does not assert a new realization/vector run.
// W1–W6, W8 and set-based admission retain -007. Historical construction comments follow.
// REALIZATION-CHECK-FORM-W1-W8-007 — PROPOSED correction for independent K8 and K9.
// SUPERSEDES -006 SHA256 12C5BC5C63C4EE10422DD0ECC1B130AD77DCEE2DBCC1ACED1B19533873C60FB0.
// W2 counts authority-bearing seed declarations using the native line-local @ guard.
// W8 is admission of the cells listed, not a requirement to populate all 105 coordinates.
// A partial walk with matching terminal declarations and PENDING cells may HOLD every W-test.
// The chart/remaining-cell observations are retained beside admission; they never replace it.
// Historical -006 source comments below describe its construction; this header records the correction.
// No geometry, Tang run, engine change, promotion, or seal change is required.
// REALIZATION-CHECK-FORM-W1-W8-006 — PROPOSED, adds internal motif admission and closure.
// BASE 210C28EB… unchanged on disk. W1–W7 retained; header below records their genealogy.
// Walk skill SHA256 D975A1BA59A7BED9DECF513DE1732637FE8D99AB381ECE312559D31F20EF728E.
// Native source SHA256 DE2FF506B89D9848BC3CA714D99C80A5675B444FB9C34DE3AA189512FE46EB63.
// Walk listing: metis-walk skill; admission is SET-based. Order is observation only.
// Rank-1 commits precede WHENCE; every commit checks its actual parents, membership and uniqueness.
// Native route data is copied from the existing source; generated entries carry IF_THEN (-010) where native still prints the retired label.
// No W result takes its value from order observations. No absent W7 witness is filled by W8.
// Complete chart: 45 seed cells + 60 derived = 105, plus 15 atoms outside the lattice.
// Missing support leaves PENDING; a contradicted declared terminal gives NO.
// Native law scope is the four recognized walk laws; other authored laws remain unread here.
// BASE W1–W7: proposed obligation-discharge reading retained from -005.
// SUPERSEDES: -004 (10DDA425CDD67107AF0D91DCF8F04F1D5D8C5B43EFEC9DE5E5AFDB159BB7C983).
// STATUS: PROPOSED. Codex holds PROPOSE; Devon Generally holds DECIDE / PROMOTE.
// W1..W6 retain -004's mechanical readings. Historical versions remain byte-unchanged.
// Each declaration carries one INPUT_IDENTITY obligation per argument and one EXPECTED_OUTPUT
// obligation. The operation name does not select a discharge rule. The state retains the
// obligations, their source spans, witnesses and remaining work in realization_obligations.
// SELF := the exact two-token argument "this file"; witness := captured input bytes.
// A bare sha256 line witnesses the sole named argument in its declaration. Two or more named
// arguments require an association witness not implemented here; counting hashes does not bind them.
// SHA256_IDENTITY_DECLARATION defines the named input identity; it does not witness a later read
// of that external file. External byte recomputation remains a separate reader obligation.
// A line ending in a reading name supplies its opcode: IF_THEN 19, NO 0, NOT_SAME 3, MAYBE 21.
// Conflicting identity claims for the sole named argument or conflicting expected reading claims
// are witnessed exclusions (NO). Missing identity / association / expected-output evidence is MAYBE.
// These proposed source-reading rules do not execute declared vectors or discharge W8.
// W-test vocabulary (-010): IF_THEN / NO / MAYBE, column R per test. Column D is the W8 route table.
// W7 meet: no declarations or SOME declaration NO -> NO; otherwise SOME MAYBE -> MAYBE;
// EVERY declaration IF_THEN -> IF_THEN. SOME W1..W7 NO -> executed byte 0; otherwise W7 MAYBE ->
// W7_MAYBE remains unresolved; -006 now computes W8 and the final meet below.
// MECHANICAL READINGS of 002 lines 155-169 (PROPOSED; REALIZE every reading, add NO behavior):
//   comments: "//" to end of line. code: everything else. tokens: identifiers and ( ) , : = ; { }
//   W1 header: the input begins "// SPEC-" (identifier); "STATUS:", "AUTHORITY:", "VERSION:" occur
//      before the first code byte.
//   W2 exactly ONE seed block (the "{ ... }" after the identifier "seed"); each comma-separated
//      entry is WITNESS ( OPERATOR ), WITNESS in {WHAT, HOW, FOR_WHAT}, or a bare OPERATOR (a
//      carrier atom), OPERATOR one of the 15; NO entry repeats.
//   W3 every seed cell is followed by a "//" reading before the end of its line.
//   W4 each of the four walk laws occurs as a law statement, token for token, as 002 writes it.
//   W5 every law statement is one of the four, each once.
//   W6 terminal section := the comment lines from the one carrying "EXPECTED TERMINAL" to the next
//      rule line ("// -") after content, or to a line with no comment. INSIDE it, declared with
//      values: "seed cells N" (N := the walk cells of the seed block), "derived N" (N := the cells
//      the four walk laws derive from them), "O_exec = " and "O_next = " each followed by "empty"
//      or a closed "{ ... }". The walk seed set := the ONE seed block, every entry in walk form;
//      a named-clause package establishes none. IF the walk seed set is partial (SOME of the
//      45 cells absent) THEN the section names PENDING cells.
//   W7 source scope: comment lines from first-token VECTORS to the next non-comment line.
//      First-token Vn introduces a declaration. Arguments are source spans inside its leading
//      call, separated by top-level commas. Each opens an identity obligation, independently
//      of the operation name. Other source forms retain unresolved argument/output obligations.
//      No header, explanatory keyword, or companion file silently supplies a witness.
// Generated from the operator / witness / law tables by an authoring script.

